    <code>segmentIndexAt</code> finds the playing segment by binary search, so seeking is cheap even for long programs. Seeking past the end returns the final position, and <code>toolAt</code> then reports the last tool. Playback time is a visual estimate based on programmed feeds; it ignores machine acceleration, so a real machine takes longer.
  </section>

  <section id="viewport-practices" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Viewport practices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Convert at the edge: store and compute in millimetres and radians, and format only for display with <code>formatLength</code> and <code>formatAngle</code>.</li>
      <li>Never reuse a parsed length after <code>parseLength</code> returns <code>undefined</code>; keep the previous value and show a validation hint.</li>
      <li>When adding a drawing tool, register it in the tool factory table so the toolbar, shortcuts, and tests address it by the same ID.</li>
      <li>Keep snap candidate queries spatial. Passing every entity to <code>findSnap</code> on each pointer move defeats the index.</li>
      <li>Treat playback duration as a preview, not a cycle-time quote.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

    <section id="spatial-index" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Hit-testing at scale: the spatial grid</h2>
    <p>The 2D editor targets 60 fps with 10,000 entities, so hit-testing and culling never scan every entity per pointer event. <code>viewport/spatial/grid.ts</code> keeps a uniform grid: each item is registered in every cell its bounding box touches, and a query returns all items whose bounds intersect the query box, in insertion order. The result is exact, never a sample.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Default cell size</td><td>50 world units (mm)</td><td>Suits a drawing about 1 m across</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Minimum cell size</td><td>1e-6</td><td>Guards against a zero or negative size, which would loop forever</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cells per item limit</td><td>4,096</td><td>Larger items (a long line across the sheet) are tracked aside instead of per cell</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>build(items)</code></td><td>Rebuild from scratch</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>upsert(id, item)</code></td><td>Insert or replace one item by id</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>remove(id)</code></td><td>Remove; unknown ids are ignored</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>query(bounds)</code></td><td>Ids whose bounds intersect the box</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 400 220" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Uniform grid index" style="max-width:400px;font:11px system-ui">
<g stroke="currentColor" opacity=".25"><path d="M20 10V210"/><path d="M80 10V210"/><path d="M140 10V210"/><path d="M200 10V210"/><path d="M260 10V210"/><path d="M320 10V210"/><path d="M380 10V210"/><path d="M20 10H380"/><path d="M20 60H380"/><path d="M20 110H380"/><path d="M20 160H380"/><path d="M20 210H380"/></g>
<g fill="none" stroke-width="1.5"><rect x="95" y="70" width="80" height="40" stroke="#3b82f6"/><circle cx="290" cy="150" r="25" stroke="#3fb37f"/><path d="M30 200L370 20" stroke="#c070e0"/><rect x="190" y="55" width="100" height="70" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/></g>
<g fill="currentColor"><text x="195" y="50">query box</text><text x="100" y="65" fill="#3b82f6">entity A</text><text x="300" y="185" fill="#3fb37f">B</text><text x="330" y="45" fill="#c070e0">long line</text></g></svg>
    <p>Cells touched by the dashed query box are visited; A and the long line are returned because their bounds intersect it, B is not.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="mesh-queue" class="doc-section">
    <h2>3D meshing queue</h2>
    <p>Solids are meshed in a Web Worker so the UI thread never blocks. <code>MeshWorkerQueue</code> in <code>view3d/mesh-jobs.ts</code> runs one job at a time:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Value</th><th>Message on failure</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Capacity (queued + running)</td><td>128</td><td>The 3D mesh queue is full. Reduce the scene complexity.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Timeout per job</td><td>15 s</td><td>3D meshing timed out. Reduce the scene complexity.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Worker error</td><td>—</td><td>The worker's message, or "The mesh worker stopped unexpectedly."</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Undecodable reply</td><td>—</td><td>The mesh worker could not decode its response.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bad geometry</td><td>positions must be <code>Float32Array</code>, indices <code>Uint32Array</code></td><td>The mesh worker returned invalid geometry.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Any failure terminates the worker and clears the whole queue, so stale scene work never lands after a newer edit; the next submission starts a fresh worker. Replies are matched by job id, so a late answer from a terminated worker is ignored.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="editor-tools" class="doc-section">
    <h2>2D tool implementations</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Tools</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>tools/two-point.ts</code></td><td>line, rectangle, circle by diameter, ellipse</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/chained.ts</code></td><td>polyline, three-point arc</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/fillet-chamfer.ts</code></td><td>round or bevel the corner between two lines</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/offset.ts</code></td><td>offset a polyline, rectangle, circle or arc by a distance</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/trim.ts</code></td><td>trim and extend</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/select.ts</code></td><td>click, box and add/remove selection</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools/annotation-transform.ts</code></td><td>move and transform annotations</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Each tool is a small state machine with <code>onPointerDown</code>, <code>onPointerMove</code> and <code>onPointerUp</code>, created by a factory in <code>tools/index.ts</code>, one per palette entry. Pointer positions pass through <code>snap-pipeline.ts</code> before a tool sees them.</p>
  </section>

